{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLSystemLayoutV17topSystemDistanceSdSgvp","title":"topSystemDistance","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"topSystemDistance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout\/topsystemdistance"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The vertical distance from the page’s top margin to the top line of the first system, in tenths. Ignored for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"all but the first system on a page.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout\/topSystemDistance"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"topSystemDistance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<top-system-distance>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system is a group of staves that are read and played simultaneously. System layout includes left and right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"margins and the vertical distance from the previous system. The system distance is measured from the bottom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line of the previous system to the top line of the current system. It is ignored for the first system on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"page. The top system distance is measured from the page’s top margin to the top line of the first system. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is ignored for all but the first system on a page."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLSystemLayout","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout/topSystemDistance":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout\/topsystemdistance","title":"topSystemDistance","abstract":[{"text":"The vertical distance from the page’s top margin to the top line of the first system, in tenths. Ignored for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"all but the first system on a page.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout\/topSystemDistance","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"topSystemDistance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"title":"MXLTenths","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the middle of a staff line."}]}}}